#. Plugin Name of the plugin
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php
msgid "ACW Maintenance Mode by Page"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php
msgid "Put your site in maintenance mode showing visitors a single page of your choice, picked from your existing pages. Choose which user roles keep browsing the whole site."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php
msgid "A Cup of Web"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php
msgid "https://www.acupofweb.it/"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:225
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:266
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:310
msgid "The site is undergoing maintenance. Please come back soon."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:226
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:957
msgid "Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:956
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1084
msgid "Maintenance Mode"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1022
msgid "The selected page must be a published page without password and cannot be the posts page."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1057
msgid "Maintenance mode is active but the selected page is not available: visitors see a generic maintenance message."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1058
msgid "Choose a page"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1088
msgid "Maintenance mode is ACTIVE."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1089
msgid "Visitors and users without access only see the selected page."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1093
msgid "Maintenance mode is ACTIVE, but no valid page is selected."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1094
msgid "Visitors see a generic maintenance message. Choose a published page."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1102
msgid "Enable maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1106
msgid "Show visitors only the selected page"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1112
msgid "Page to display"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1116
msgid "— Select a page —"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1123
msgid "Choose one of the published pages listed under “Pages” (the posts page and password-protected pages cannot be used)."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1127
msgid "Who can browse the site"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1142
msgid "Checked roles keep browsing the site and using the dashboard. Everyone else, including logged-out visitors, only sees the maintenance page. Administrators always have access."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1147
msgid "Pages always reachable"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1155
msgid "Pages that stay reachable during maintenance, such as a front-end login, registration or account page. Hold Ctrl (Cmd on Mac) to select more than one."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of page titles.
#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1161
#, php-format
msgid "Detected automatically and always reachable: %s"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1170
msgid "Popups and other plugin elements"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1174
msgid "Do not show popups, chat buttons, bars and other elements that plugins add to every page"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1176
msgid "Keeps out of the maintenance page popups and slide-ins (e.g. Hustle, Popup Maker, OptinMonster), chat and WhatsApp buttons, notice and cookie bars, share buttons, ads and opt-in forms added after the content. The plugins used to build the page keep working: those of its blocks, of its shortcodes and of the page builder (e.g. Elementor)."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1177
msgid "Recommended. Uncheck it if you want an element on the maintenance page, such as a floating WhatsApp button. Tracking codes are handled by the next option."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1182
msgid "Hide the Elementor popups and floating buttons too, also when the page is built with Elementor"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1185
msgid "Covers the popups of Elementor Pro and the floating buttons and bars of Elementor (e.g. a WhatsApp button). Uncheck it to keep them on the maintenance page, for example a popup opened by a button in the page. It works only together with the option above: when that one is unchecked, every popup is shown."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1193
msgid "Tracking codes"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1197
msgid "Do not load tracking codes on the maintenance page"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1199
msgid "Removes the scripts added to the site by plugins or by hand, such as Google Analytics, Tag Manager, Facebook Pixel or the cookie banner, so visits to the maintenance page are not tracked. The page keeps its look: the styles and the scripts of WordPress, of the theme and of the blocks, shortcodes and page builder used in the page are still loaded."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1200
msgid "Recommended on a staging site or on a site not online yet. On a live site you can leave it unchecked, to keep counting visits. If something in the page stops working (e.g. a captcha added to a form by another plugin), leave it unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1204
msgid "REST API"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1208
msgid "Hide pages, posts and other content from the REST API to visitors who are not signed in"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1210
msgid "During maintenance, the content of the site can still be read at addresses such as /wp-json/wp/v2/pages. When checked, these addresses answer “temporarily unavailable” to visitors who are not signed in. Signed-in users and connections with an application password keep working, and so do the forms of other plugins."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1211
msgid "Recommended on a staging site or when the content is not public yet. Leave it unchecked if apps or external services read the site content."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1215
msgid "Content width"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1220
msgid "Default width (inherited from the theme)"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1225
msgid "Full width"
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1232
msgid "Saving purges the cache of SiteGround Speed Optimizer, WP Rocket, LiteSpeed Cache, W3 Total Cache, WP Super Cache and WP Fastest Cache. With other caching plugins, a CDN or a server cache, purge it manually after turning maintenance on or off."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1235
msgid "During maintenance the XML sitemaps answer “temporarily unavailable” as well, while robots.txt stays reachable: this way search engines see that the pause is temporary."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1238
msgid "This is a maintenance mode, not a security barrier: direct media file URLs stay reachable, and so does the REST API unless you hide it above."
msgstr ""

#: acw-maintenance-mode-by-page.php:1255
msgid "⚠ Maintenance active"
msgstr ""
